TASK A5 – DESIGN RECOVERY AND RETHROWING (4 Marks)
A5.1 – Where to Catch (2 Marks)
Exceptions should be caught at different levels depending on the responsibility of the function.
- Billing functions: Detect invalid data and throw appropriate exceptions.
- Service layer: Catch exceptions, log the error details and rethrow using throw; when further handling is required.
- Main function: Catch exceptions, display a clear error message to the user and prevent the program from crashing.
Example:
try {
    processBill();
}
catch (const BillingError& e) {
    std::cout << "Billing error: " << e.what();
    throw;
}


The throw; statement rethrows the same exception without changing its original type.
A5.2 – No Leaks on Errors (2 Marks)
Stack unwinding is the process in which local objects are automatically destroyed when an exception is thrown and control moves to a matching catch block.

RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization) uses constructors and destructors to manage resources automatically. Objects such as std::unique_ptr, std::vector and file objects release resources when they go out of scope.

Therefore, RAII prevents memory leaks and ensures resources are released even when exceptions occur.

Predict the Output
Predicted Output:
